Since $(y-w)^2 = n - 4x \ge 0$, we have $n - 4x = \sqrt{n}$, so $(y-w)^2 = \sqrt{n}$, requiring **$\sqrt{n}$ to be a perfect square**, i.e., $n = k^4$.

