## Constructing the Sidon Set (Greedy Argument)

Given the residue counts $(c_0, c_1, c_2, c_3) = (315, 336, 315, 330)$, we construct the Sidon set greedily. Assign each $a_i$ a target residue $r_i \pmod{4}$ (with the right multiplicities). At step $k$, having chosen $a_1 < \cdots < a_{k-1}$ with all pairwise sums distinct, we select $a_k > a_{k-1}$ with $a_k \equiv r_k \pmod 4$ avoiding:

