There are at most $(k-1)\binom{k-1}{2} = O(k^3)$ forbidden values — finitely many. Since infinitely many integers have residue $r_k \pmod 4$, we can always find a valid $a_k$. The greedy construction never stalls, producing a valid Sidon set with the prescribed residue distribution.

